1
00:02:03,570 --> 00:02:08,610
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING THE
FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

2
00:02:08,610 --> 00:02:20,010
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:03:11,220 --> 00:03:13,770
Most of the soldiers Osman killed…

4
00:03:16,050 --> 00:03:18,020
… are torn into pieces by wild animals.

5
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:20,480
What about these ones?

6
00:03:21,370 --> 00:03:25,050
For the ceremony, we brought the ones
who were still one piece.

7
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:31,450
All of them gave their lives for my son.

8
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:40,420
They are now my children who will live
till the infinity and beyond.

9
00:03:48,850 --> 00:03:51,140
We are looking for their murderers,
Geyhatu.

10
00:03:52,340 --> 00:03:53,850
Their souls will be honored.

11
00:03:55,420 --> 00:03:57,910
We will save Möngke.

12
00:03:58,510 --> 00:03:59,420
Osman!

13
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:06,600
Osman!

14
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:15,880
Blood!

15
00:04:17,079 --> 00:04:18,250
Erlik Khan…

16
00:04:20,110 --> 00:04:22,740
… they got killed for my son.

17
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:25,140
Honor their souls!

18
00:04:25,680 --> 00:04:29,020
Wipe out and curse all those murderers!

19
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:31,600
Oh, Erlik Khan!

20
00:04:32,310 --> 00:04:34,850
Your black mount!

21
00:04:35,220 --> 00:04:37,800
Your black rein!

22
00:04:38,450 --> 00:04:40,400
Your whip, a black snake!

23
00:04:40,570 --> 00:04:43,340
You are the mightiest of all!

24
00:04:43,340 --> 00:04:44,820
Oh, Erlik Khan!

25
00:04:44,940 --> 00:04:47,650
Take the souls of my soldiers.

26
00:04:47,970 --> 00:04:52,600
Give me my son, oh Erlik Khan!

27
00:04:56,340 --> 00:04:57,620
Wait for me, Kayı.

28
00:04:58,220 --> 00:05:01,140
I’m coming to terrorize you all!

29
00:05:48,770 --> 00:05:53,250
My Bey, I understand you want to come to
terms with Nikola.

30
00:05:54,310 --> 00:05:55,250
However…

31
00:05:55,770 --> 00:06:01,110
…don’t you think these conditions are too
harsh for both sides?

32
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:06,450
An eye for an eyes is Fardh for the
sons of Abraham, Dündar

33
00:06:07,170 --> 00:06:10,420
Whether a christian or a jew..

34
00:06:12,050 --> 00:06:13,480
… none can reject.

35
00:06:14,740 --> 00:06:18,680
Also, those terms related to concessions
about trading…

36
00:06:18,880 --> 00:06:21,740
… and the safety of merchants...

37
00:06:23,540 --> 00:06:26,140
... will drive him into a corner.

38
00:06:26,140 --> 00:06:28,020
None can question your words, my Bey.

39
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:29,850
You know better than me.

40
00:06:30,570 --> 00:06:33,000
As long as you feed a snake in its pit...

41
00:06:34,450 --> 00:06:36,450
… it won’t try to bite you.

42
00:06:37,850 --> 00:06:40,880
Till we are completely done with the
terrors of Geyhatu…

43
00:06:41,110 --> 00:06:44,680
… you will keep Nikola busy with this
agreement.

44
00:06:45,650 --> 00:06:47,540
It’s your duty as the ambassador.

45
00:06:48,650 --> 00:06:49,680
Do you understand?

46
00:06:51,310 --> 00:06:55,050
We will do what's necessary once this
trouble ends.

47
00:06:56,050 --> 00:06:58,940
As long as we have Allah with us.

48
00:06:59,450 --> 00:07:02,510
Has Gündüz left for Kulacahisar?

49
00:07:02,650 --> 00:07:04,710
He left after the morning prayer, my Bey.

50
00:07:09,310 --> 00:07:11,480
Spit it out, Dündar.

51
00:07:16,280 --> 00:07:17,240
My Bey…

52
00:07:19,170 --> 00:07:25,020
… why are you keeping my Osman away
from this?

53
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:30,200
That path is harsh and long…

54
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:34,940
… sometimes one will have to stop and
get rest…

55
00:07:35,310 --> 00:07:40,770
… so that he will get his strength and
mind back.

56
00:07:44,910 --> 00:07:46,170
May you live long, My Bey.

57
00:07:48,220 --> 00:07:51,710
May Allah never take you from us.

58
00:08:26,770 --> 00:08:29,770
Apprentice, where have you been?

59
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:31,620
I haven’t seen you in the workshop.

60
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:34,250
Let him be free today, Davut Usta.

61
00:08:35,419 --> 00:08:36,400
A day is nothing.

62
00:08:38,110 --> 00:08:39,880
Only for your sake, my Osman Bey.

63
00:08:42,679 --> 00:08:44,800
Come on then!

64
00:08:44,970 --> 00:08:46,940
Let the people see some real archery!

65
00:09:26,370 --> 00:09:27,620
Swing it!

66
00:09:47,110 --> 00:09:48,020
Swing!

67
00:10:03,850 --> 00:10:04,740
Swing!

68
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:39,110
The arrow has left the bow.

69
00:10:40,280 --> 00:10:42,080
May it be for good.

70
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:23,220
Since when these elegant eyes started to
fill with sorrow…

71
00:11:23,220 --> 00:11:24,600
… while I’m off duty, Hatun?

72
00:11:33,110 --> 00:11:36,820
I saw you fighting with hundreds of
enemies and my eyes didn’t even move once.

73
00:11:41,050 --> 00:11:43,110
This duty of yours isn’t fighting, my Bey.

74
00:11:45,510 --> 00:11:50,110
Your destination is the Devil’s pit.

75
00:11:52,170 --> 00:11:54,600
My father gave me a very important
duty, Hatun.

76
00:11:55,820 --> 00:11:59,340
Not only the people in our Tent but also
the people in other Tents...

77
00:12:00,740 --> 00:12:03,820
… ,as well as all the Anatolian
Greeks, have held their breath…

78
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:06,940
… waiting for the message, I’m going to
bring.

79
00:12:07,220 --> 00:12:08,650
This is what I fear, my Savcı.

80
00:12:09,570 --> 00:12:13,680
Your father gave you the mission to
stop a whole army by yourself.

81
00:12:17,110 --> 00:12:21,020
Why do those tyrants are coming at us?

82
00:12:23,250 --> 00:12:28,000
Geyhatu thinks that Osman has
captured, his son, Möngke.

83
00:12:29,310 --> 00:12:31,220
Because of this, he wants to attack us.

84
00:12:33,250 --> 00:12:37,020
Which snake’s pit, Osman Bey stuck his
stick this time?

85
00:12:39,370 --> 00:12:41,850
My brother, Osman, is being accused
for no reason.

86
00:12:42,050 --> 00:12:45,200
You are the one who is solving the problem
he brought upon us.

87
00:12:45,880 --> 00:12:47,480
Those men are tyrants.

88
00:12:50,740 --> 00:12:52,220
What if they try to kill you?

89
00:12:54,140 --> 00:12:55,050
I will be doomed.

90
00:12:57,170 --> 00:12:58,740
And miserable, my Savcı.

91
00:13:00,420 --> 00:13:02,820
If he is the grandson of Genghis Khan…

92
00:13:04,650 --> 00:13:07,280
… I’m the son of Ertugrul, Hatun.

93
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:13,000
My father has handed me the safety of
these lands.

94
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:19,940
Your duty is not the think of my life
and safety but my victory.

95
00:13:24,800 --> 00:13:25,800
Do you understand?

96
00:13:37,740 --> 00:13:39,450
Our future is in your hands.

97
00:13:41,220 --> 00:13:42,650
I’m proud of you.

98
00:13:56,050 --> 00:13:57,170
Allah is eternal!

99
00:13:57,850 --> 00:13:58,880
Allah is the truth!

100
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:00,850
Allah is eternal!

101
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:02,370
Allah is the truth!

102
00:14:02,650 --> 00:14:03,770
Allah is eternal!

103
00:14:03,910 --> 00:14:04,910
Allah is the truth!

104
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:05,970
Allah is eternal!

105
00:14:06,170 --> 00:14:08,080
-Allah is the truth!
-Allah is eternal!

106
00:14:13,820 --> 00:14:15,540
The fire is calling for you, my Bey.

107
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:16,710
Do you hear it?

108
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:24,170
It would be ashamed of itself, if it
knew about the fire in me.

109
00:14:24,850 --> 00:14:26,970
Sorrow will be gone, only when it’s
shared.

110
00:14:28,250 --> 00:14:30,800
And the flame gets stronger when
more fuel added.

111
00:14:32,110 --> 00:14:33,970
I’m waiting for the time it dies down.

112
00:14:38,710 --> 00:14:42,570
-May Allah be with you, my Bey.
-Thank you.

113
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:09,650
Don’t let this flag end up on the floor
even if Geyhatu takes your head.

114
00:16:09,740 --> 00:16:11,450
Oguz’s head may drop on the floor…

115
00:16:11,480 --> 00:16:14,650
… but his honor always stands
straight just like the minaret.

116
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:16,080
Don't you worry.

117
00:16:19,940 --> 00:16:23,940
We will fight but Allah is the one who
makes us victorious.

118
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:27,880
Our Tent’s future is in your hands, son.

119
00:16:29,510 --> 00:16:32,600
You must find a way to stop Geyhatu.

120
00:16:33,820 --> 00:16:35,620
Don’t you forget about this.

121
00:16:35,910 --> 00:16:37,510
I will never do that, Bey Father.

122
00:16:38,450 --> 00:16:41,150
With Allah’s permission, I will get rid
of this trouble.

123
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:51,880
May Allah protect you.

124
00:16:52,420 --> 00:16:53,670
May you live long, my Bey.

125
00:17:10,220 --> 00:17:12,140
We will be waiting for your good news.

126
00:17:12,310 --> 00:17:13,569
May you live long, uncle.

127
00:17:28,310 --> 00:17:29,600
Brother…

128
00:17:31,140 --> 00:17:32,600
… your duty is tough.

129
00:17:33,710 --> 00:17:35,420
You will enter the pit of snakes.

130
00:17:36,850 --> 00:17:38,340
May Allah help you.

131
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:40,170
May you live long, brother.

132
00:17:40,880 --> 00:17:43,400
Once I’m here, we will train together.

133
00:19:54,570 --> 00:19:56,910
Horses are ready, my Bey.

134
00:19:58,110 --> 00:19:59,540
Did anybody see you?

135
00:19:59,620 --> 00:20:00,850
No, my Bey.

136
00:20:03,650 --> 00:20:05,400
Then, may Allah help us.

137
00:20:06,570 --> 00:20:09,820
My Bey, what if Ertugrul Bey understands?

138
00:20:10,970 --> 00:20:15,850
Our life and our swords belong to no one
but Ertugrul Bey.

139
00:20:16,340 --> 00:20:20,310
But, if stop following Osman Bey’s
path, our cause will be in danger.

140
00:20:23,280 --> 00:20:24,340
Let’s go.

141
00:20:28,170 --> 00:20:29,220
Osman!

142
00:20:53,940 --> 00:20:55,490
I know what you are about to do.

143
00:20:55,850 --> 00:20:57,200
So, you know I won’t stop.

144
00:20:58,220 --> 00:20:59,600
Who’s telling you to stop?

145
00:22:55,280 --> 00:22:56,560
It is time.

146
00:23:50,120 --> 00:23:53,120
It seems that Ertuğrul Bey is
quite displeased with me.

147
00:23:53,560 --> 00:23:57,000
Since he sent you instead.

148
00:24:00,440 --> 00:24:02,880
What you’re doing is dangerous, Nikola.

149
00:24:04,920 --> 00:24:09,280
I’ve come to your
castle to visit and then…

150
00:24:09,280 --> 00:24:14,120
… discuss the agreement.

151
00:24:23,080 --> 00:24:27,880
Could the fact that Geyhatu’s armies
are marching towards you…

152
00:24:27,880 --> 00:24:33,440
… be the reason why
Ertuğrul Bey sent you instead?

153
00:24:33,440 --> 00:24:35,440
Dündar Bey?

154
00:24:38,920 --> 00:24:40,240
Dündar Bey…

155
00:24:40,680 --> 00:24:45,360
If you think I’m unaware of
all the things happening…

156
00:24:45,880 --> 00:24:49,080
… that means you’re greatly mistaken.

157
00:25:30,360 --> 00:25:32,360
What gives, my Osman?

158
00:25:34,320 --> 00:25:37,320
Did you get lost in the forest?

159
00:25:39,880 --> 00:25:41,360
Osman…

160
00:25:50,560 --> 00:25:52,320
Where are you Alps?

161
00:25:52,320 --> 00:25:54,320
Are you out hunting by yourself?

162
00:25:54,960 --> 00:25:57,440
I couldn’t let my brother
hunt infidels alone.

163
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:01,960
So, I also came.

164
00:26:02,520 --> 00:26:04,400
Were you afraid of losing your pray?

165
00:26:06,240 --> 00:26:09,040
When did my brother
ever let an infidel run away?

166
00:26:35,320 --> 00:26:37,560
You’ll go back to the tent, Osman.

167
00:26:38,280 --> 00:26:42,040
Brother. Let me come with you.

168
00:26:42,040 --> 00:26:45,560
If my father wanted you to come…

169
00:26:45,560 --> 00:26:49,380
… he would have given you duty as well.
Right, brother?

170
00:26:49,840 --> 00:26:54,120
Allow me to come to
Geyhatu’s Tent with you.

171
00:26:54,120 --> 00:26:56,680
What the man wants is to kill you.

172
00:26:56,680 --> 00:27:00,920
Brother! I’m afraid something
will happen to you because of me!

173
00:27:00,920 --> 00:27:06,520
What if something happens to you?

174
00:27:10,400 --> 00:27:13,080
What will I tell my father then, Osman?

175
00:27:15,040 --> 00:27:16,680
Answer, brother!

176
00:27:17,400 --> 00:27:18,680
What will I tell him?

177
00:27:19,400 --> 00:27:21,640
Did you ever think about this?

178
00:27:22,160 --> 00:27:23,720
What will I tell him?

179
00:27:25,800 --> 00:27:29,360
You’re done for if my father finds
out that you did this.

180
00:27:34,880 --> 00:27:37,790
I’ve been fighting the Mongols
since last year, brother.

181
00:27:38,080 --> 00:27:41,640
I know what they think and how they feel.

182
00:27:43,720 --> 00:27:48,000
Geyhatu will learn the truth
if he listens to me.

183
00:27:49,360 --> 00:27:50,440
I’m coming with you.

184
00:27:50,440 --> 00:27:52,320
Osman!

185
00:27:52,800 --> 00:27:55,000
Enough! Go back to the Tent.

186
00:27:55,280 --> 00:27:56,640
I will not!

187
00:28:06,920 --> 00:28:17,520
I wonder. While we’re fighting a plague,
you’ve come to the Tent and raised hell.

188
00:28:18,320 --> 00:28:21,080
You’ve shed the blood of our Alps.

189
00:28:21,080 --> 00:28:24,880
Is this the way you see peace?

190
00:28:24,880 --> 00:28:28,320
Is this the friendship you’re offering?

191
00:28:28,320 --> 00:28:33,480
Didn’t Savcı Bey enter my lands
and steal my ammunition?

192
00:28:33,840 --> 00:28:36,400
Didn’t he kill my soldiers?

193
00:28:39,560 --> 00:28:41,360
Dündar Bey…

194
00:28:41,360 --> 00:28:45,200
If someone’s going to
call someone account for…

195
00:28:45,200 --> 00:28:47,200
… that’s me.

196
00:28:47,640 --> 00:28:54,720
What are you even doing with
the Mongol’s flying fire?

197
00:28:54,720 --> 00:28:56,720
I like to take precautions.

198
00:28:56,960 --> 00:28:58,360
Yes, precautions.

199
00:28:58,360 --> 00:29:01,160
What precautions? Governor Nikola?

200
00:29:01,880 --> 00:29:07,200
You expected us to go for your lands
while we’re dealing with Mongols?

201
00:29:08,160 --> 00:29:13,840
You’re trying to take the revenge of
the past with Mongols as an excuse.

202
00:29:14,320 --> 00:29:16,760
Tell me. What are you up to?

203
00:29:17,640 --> 00:29:20,920
Kulacahisar or Söğüt?

204
00:29:20,920 --> 00:29:23,600
I just want peace.

205
00:29:23,600 --> 00:29:30,680
But remember, Dündar Bey. Osman came and
took Kulacahisar in your most desperate times.

206
00:29:32,600 --> 00:29:36,920
Why and how should I trust you?

207
00:29:37,480 --> 00:29:39,920
Shouldn’t I take any precautions?

208
00:29:57,720 --> 00:30:02,080
Trust is mutual, Nikola.

209
00:30:02,080 --> 00:30:08,520
If you still want peace,
you will obey the rules.

210
00:30:10,760 --> 00:30:16,760
Then there’s only one rule.

211
00:30:23,120 --> 00:30:25,320
An eye for an eye.

212
00:30:26,120 --> 00:30:27,520
Be frank!

213
00:30:28,800 --> 00:30:33,000
As it’s written on your
holy book, Dündar Bey.

214
00:30:34,040 --> 00:30:44,160
Believers! Retribution is prescribed
for you in cases of killing.

215
00:30:46,760 --> 00:30:49,760
If a freeman is guilty then the freeman.

216
00:30:50,320 --> 00:30:53,560
If a slave is guilty then the slave.

217
00:30:54,400 --> 00:30:57,640
If a female is guilty, then the female.

218
00:31:02,000 --> 00:31:04,640
Looks like you did your homework, Nikola.

219
00:31:10,920 --> 00:31:13,560
As it’s written in your book.

220
00:31:14,160 --> 00:31:22,440
Treat people the way you
want to be treated.

221
00:31:23,760 --> 00:31:25,600
Correct?

222
00:31:25,600 --> 00:31:27,600
Correct.

223
00:31:28,040 --> 00:31:33,320
Then, if you plant seeds of
evil to the garden of peace…

224
00:31:33,320 --> 00:31:35,320
… you harvest evil.

225
00:31:36,240 --> 00:31:39,040
If you plant seeds of evil…

226
00:31:39,040 --> 00:31:43,200
… you pay the price for it.

227
00:31:44,080 --> 00:31:47,200
Is this also valid for Ertuğrul Bey?

228
00:31:47,480 --> 00:31:52,480
Everyone pays for what they
did during peaceful times.

229
00:31:53,640 --> 00:31:58,880
No one should make promises
they won’t be able to keep, Nikola.

230
00:32:01,520 --> 00:32:11,720
Ertuğrul Bey wrote and stated the article
you’re so excited about beforehand.

231
00:32:12,840 --> 00:32:15,760
And we say…

232
00:32:16,360 --> 00:32:19,720
… an eye for an eye.

233
00:32:28,760 --> 00:32:31,880
An eye for an eye.

234
00:32:35,960 --> 00:32:37,560
Alps!

235
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:42,160
Contain Osman Bey!

236
00:32:48,160 --> 00:32:50,000
Don’t, brother!

237
00:32:51,960 --> 00:32:55,160
I’m talking to you, Alps! Now!

238
00:32:58,680 --> 00:33:01,680
My Allah, don’t make me do this!

239
00:33:05,480 --> 00:33:06,600
Brother!

240
00:33:08,320 --> 00:33:09,960
Don’t!

241
00:33:13,520 --> 00:33:15,680
He doesn’t listen to his Bey!

242
00:33:16,200 --> 00:33:18,480
He doesn’t listen to his father!

243
00:33:18,480 --> 00:33:22,200
He doesn’t listen to his brother.
What have you become, Osman?

244
00:33:23,240 --> 00:33:24,560
Alps!

245
00:33:24,560 --> 00:33:27,240
Don’t Savcı Bey, don’t!

246
00:33:53,680 --> 00:34:00,880
I know that I can trust your word as much
as I trust my Emperor’ss word, Dündar Bey.

247
00:34:00,880 --> 00:34:06,480
We’ll see that together, Nikola.

248
00:34:14,440 --> 00:34:17,360
Alps! Take him.

249
00:34:30,639 --> 00:34:32,719
Don’t make me do these, brother!

250
00:34:36,520 --> 00:34:39,600
Geyhatu wants me, not you!

251
00:34:41,159 --> 00:34:44,560
I killed both Balgay and Subutay!

252
00:34:44,560 --> 00:34:49,840
If there’s someone to settle accounts
with, that’s me! Not you!

253
00:34:51,239 --> 00:34:56,360
Oh, Osman! Oh, my brother!

254
00:34:56,360 --> 00:34:58,240
You’re blind!

255
00:34:59,200 --> 00:35:02,440
My father is trying to protect you,
don’t you see?

256
00:35:08,680 --> 00:35:11,960
Is it your job to protect me, brother?

257
00:35:11,960 --> 00:35:13,880
It is, yes!

258
00:35:13,880 --> 00:35:15,480
It is our job!

259
00:35:15,480 --> 00:35:19,400
Do you know why?
They have kidnapped Möngke!

260
00:35:19,400 --> 00:35:22,400
Geyhatu is sure that you did it!

261
00:35:23,800 --> 00:35:29,680
That’s why he’s marching
at us with his army!

262
00:35:31,960 --> 00:35:35,640
It’s because of you, brother!
You!

263
00:35:37,560 --> 00:35:39,000
It’s you.

264
00:35:48,080 --> 00:35:51,720
Someone’s using you for
their tricks, brother.

265
00:35:51,720 --> 00:35:55,240
The trap in our Tent
is bigger than you think.

266
00:35:57,920 --> 00:35:59,960
There are traps within traps, brother!

267
00:35:59,960 --> 00:36:01,440
That’s why I’m coming.

268
00:36:01,440 --> 00:36:06,000
I will face Geyhatu so that he can see
that I have nothing to do with it.

269
00:36:06,400 --> 00:36:09,880
I will come with you
whether you like it or not.

270
00:36:09,880 --> 00:36:11,800
Nothing can take me to the Tent!

271
00:36:11,800 --> 00:36:13,320
Osman!

272
00:36:22,160 --> 00:36:23,680
Father?

273
00:37:08,760 --> 00:37:13,520
Since when you don’t listen to
the word of you Bey, Osman?

274
00:37:15,800 --> 00:37:18,640
What do you mean, father?

275
00:37:18,640 --> 00:37:23,880
I’d rather get stumbled on by horses
rather than disobey the word of my Bey.

276
00:37:23,880 --> 00:37:26,160
Then what are you doing here?

277
00:37:26,160 --> 00:37:29,400
I’m here to protect my brother from
the wrath of Geyhatu, father.

278
00:37:30,400 --> 00:37:34,000
If you allow me, I want to go with him.

279
00:37:34,000 --> 00:37:37,280
Take your Alps and go back to the Tent.

280
00:37:37,280 --> 00:37:43,960
If I don’t see you when I’m at the Tent,
I don’t want to see you ever again.

281
00:37:44,720 --> 00:37:47,960
-Father--
- Osman do as I say!

282
00:38:37,480 --> 00:38:42,520
Osman is unpredictable, father. What
should I do if he comes after me again?

283
00:38:42,520 --> 00:38:46,960
The punishment of disobeying
my order is certain.

284
00:38:48,080 --> 00:38:50,000
I can make no excuses.

285
00:38:51,880 --> 00:38:56,960
You will give him the harshest
punishment if he comes again.

286
00:38:59,120 --> 00:39:01,440
As you order, my Bey.

287
00:39:02,000 --> 00:39:03,400
If you’ll excuse me…

288
00:39:21,240 --> 00:39:30,120
Let your mind be bright, your path clear,
your sword sharp, son.

289
00:39:48,240 --> 00:39:51,240
Mashallah!

290
00:39:52,480 --> 00:39:58,600
You’ve done plenty! Lena Hatun,
they always said you were hard working.

291
00:39:59,000 --> 00:40:01,040
But we didn’t expect this much!

292
00:40:03,360 --> 00:40:07,000
I didn’t do anything.
Bala is a very nimble Hatun.

293
00:40:07,640 --> 00:40:10,920
She could make supplies for
not just the Kayı…

294
00:40:10,920 --> 00:40:12,920
… but every surrounding Tents for winter.

295
00:40:14,680 --> 00:40:16,400
That’s true, I know.

296
00:40:16,400 --> 00:40:18,760
Bala Hatun is our Tent’s arms and hands.

297
00:40:18,760 --> 00:40:22,520
And Osman Bey is its eyes and ears.

298
00:40:33,920 --> 00:40:37,080
You know where Osman went, Bala.

299
00:40:43,280 --> 00:40:47,040
If Savcı finds out that Osman went
after him, it wouldn’t be good.

300
00:40:48,320 --> 00:40:50,480
How do you know that Lena?

301
00:40:50,880 --> 00:40:55,000
I know Osman as well as
I know Savcı, Bala.

302
00:40:58,240 --> 00:41:02,480
He is his brother after all. Of course
you know him.

303
00:41:04,720 --> 00:41:09,800
When it comes to his duty, Savcı doesn’t
care if someone’s his brother or not.

304
00:41:09,800 --> 00:41:11,450
What are you talking about Lena?

305
00:41:11,450 --> 00:41:22,720
Hatuns! If siblings fight
each other, we’re done for. Know that.

306
00:41:23,960 --> 00:41:28,760
The Tent went through a lot because
of those who were acting on their own.

307
00:41:32,400 --> 00:41:36,360
Bala!

308
00:41:37,880 --> 00:41:42,640
You should get a hold of Osman.

309
00:41:42,960 --> 00:41:49,320
Look. Savcı Bey isn’t
like Dündar or Gündüz.

310
00:41:50,400 --> 00:41:53,440
I see that you’re the
one fanning the flame, Hazal Hatun.

311
00:41:53,960 --> 00:41:55,160
Never!

312
00:41:56,040 --> 00:41:59,720
If you want the put out
the fire of unrest, water it.

313
00:42:01,360 --> 00:42:03,680
Can’t believe what I’m hearing.

314
00:42:16,560 --> 00:42:17,960
Osman.

315
00:43:28,840 --> 00:43:32,020
Our love suppresses
the mountain-shaking anger of yours.

316
00:43:32,020 --> 00:43:35,810
You have become
the solution to my problems.

317
00:43:36,135 --> 00:43:39,985
- I know it’s hard. - I know it’s harsh.

318
00:44:27,127 --> 00:44:30,567
Your breath is out of
order, my dear friend.

319
00:44:31,005 --> 00:44:33,445
What caused this anger?

320
00:44:33,703 --> 00:44:36,173
Falling into the trap of Ertuğrul!

321
00:44:41,594 --> 00:44:43,194
What does that mean?

322
00:44:43,866 --> 00:44:46,386
The agreement that you sealed!

323
00:44:46,828 --> 00:44:50,828
This will trap us! You are
making a mistake Nikola!

324
00:44:50,917 --> 00:44:53,147
That goatherd trapped you!

325
00:45:04,148 --> 00:45:08,878
Goatherd? The "goatherd"
that killed your father?

326
00:45:15,610 --> 00:45:20,640
Don't you talk about my
father like that again, never.

327
00:45:24,351 --> 00:45:31,071
We came here for our children's future,
Vladius, not for our fathers' revenge.

328
00:45:37,138 --> 00:45:42,358
Until I take my father's revenge,
I don't care about children's future.

329
00:45:51,537 --> 00:45:54,487
I like your restless spirit.

330
00:45:57,255 --> 00:46:02,015
But remember, Vladius, the great
warriors that passed through seas...

331
00:46:02,169 --> 00:46:05,629
... change the skies, not their souls.

332
00:46:10,646 --> 00:46:18,316
We'll show the rains of holy Byzantine to
the Turks that turned Söğüt into a swamp.

333
00:46:18,691 --> 00:46:26,181
And we will do all these with the
help of the agreement that I sealed.

334
00:47:25,226 --> 00:47:28,936
-Salaimun Alaikum
-Alaikum Salam, Bey son.

335
00:47:28,955 --> 00:47:30,315
May it be easy.

336
00:47:31,125 --> 00:47:32,905
Easier said than done.

337
00:47:36,526 --> 00:47:39,036
You are just sharpening
a knife, Kumral Abdal.

338
00:47:39,418 --> 00:47:45,068
Sharpening a knife is for everyone. Being
Ismail and making a knife is for the wise.

339
00:47:45,469 --> 00:47:48,299
Being Ismail is easy to say, hard to do.

340
00:47:52,382 --> 00:47:54,312
I heard, it's truth.

341
00:47:56,103 --> 00:47:58,163
Boran came here with haste.

342
00:47:58,165 --> 00:48:01,785
I said " Which scorpion's nest
did Bey's son disturb again?"

343
00:48:05,175 --> 00:48:06,615
Geyhatu.

344
00:48:14,841 --> 00:48:18,841
Geyhatu? Wow...

345
00:48:18,934 --> 00:48:21,554
All this rush for that weakling?

346
00:48:28,975 --> 00:48:34,835
Miserable people like us
have weak enemies like those.

347
00:48:39,978 --> 00:48:43,598
It's okay, there is always a solution.

348
00:48:44,455 --> 00:48:46,055
I am listening, Bey's son.

349
00:48:54,026 --> 00:48:57,456
There is a game inside
another game. A big one.

350
00:48:59,177 --> 00:49:01,497
My brother went to Geyhatu.

351
00:49:03,179 --> 00:49:05,729
Maybe his dead body
will come out of there.

352
00:49:07,807 --> 00:49:12,867
If all this rush is for saving your
brother, don't you bother me, Bey's son.

353
00:49:19,103 --> 00:49:22,423
If the fate is written,
no one can stand in its way.

354
00:49:28,115 --> 00:49:31,985
He wants me. They blame
me for Möngke's abduction.

355
00:49:32,511 --> 00:49:35,661
If we don't do something,
many innocent people will be hurt.

356
00:49:35,661 --> 00:49:37,341
What do you want from me?

357
00:49:37,923 --> 00:49:40,103
To be my remedy.

358
00:49:49,432 --> 00:49:53,642
Now you are talking my
language, Bey's son. I am listening.

359
00:50:01,557 --> 00:50:06,857
You know Normans the best.
You can tell me where their base is.

360
00:50:07,954 --> 00:50:11,954
We are ready with my Alps.
I will prepare the game this time.

361
00:50:59,650 --> 00:51:12,000
Blood! Blood! Blood!

362
00:51:12,668 --> 00:51:14,378
They are messengers!

363
00:51:15,232 --> 00:51:17,252
Get back, you idiots!

364
00:52:21,426 --> 00:52:23,016
Who are you?

365
00:52:23,338 --> 00:52:27,338
Savcı Bey, son of Ertuğrul Ghazi!
I came here as a messenger.

366
00:52:32,285 --> 00:52:34,255
Kill them.

367
00:52:56,902 --> 00:52:58,742
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.

368
00:53:04,637 --> 00:53:06,737
Osman isn't here yet?

369
00:53:08,444 --> 00:53:12,644
Osman rode somewhere, my Bey.
He will be here soon.

370
00:53:20,373 --> 00:53:22,603
Where is Osman, daughter?

371
00:53:25,566 --> 00:53:28,036
Can't you speak, daughter?

372
00:53:31,820 --> 00:53:34,410
Didn't he tell you where he was going?

373
00:53:35,711 --> 00:53:38,021
I wonder too, my Bey.

374
00:53:54,395 --> 00:53:59,745
As-Sirāt is thinner than a hair,
sharper than a sword.

375
00:54:00,935 --> 00:54:06,505
We don't only pass from
this bridge in afterlife.

376
00:54:06,665 --> 00:54:11,175
Sometimes, we need to
pass them in this life too.

377
00:54:12,085 --> 00:54:15,785
Those who pass them are called heroes.

378
00:54:19,729 --> 00:54:24,809
Then, what is the secret of
those who pass them, father?

379
00:54:25,924 --> 00:54:29,924
If one stays strong in the face
of disasters, control one's anger...

380
00:54:31,209 --> 00:54:37,209
... keep one's heart clean, one can
pass through As-Sirāt in this life too.

381
00:54:39,884 --> 00:54:43,884
Fortunately, my Savcı
has all those traits.

382
00:54:48,718 --> 00:54:52,718
Savcı Bey rose on our Tent like a sun.

383
00:54:53,932 --> 00:54:57,392
Long may he live. Osman Bey...

384
00:54:57,392 --> 00:55:02,602
... wouldn't leave
without a word, my Bala.

385
00:55:02,736 --> 00:55:06,736
Is there something that troubles him?

386
00:55:12,703 --> 00:55:15,923
The only thing that troubles
Osman Bey is the future of his Tent...

387
00:55:15,923 --> 00:55:17,763
Hazal Hatun, don't you know?

388
00:55:20,016 --> 00:55:21,976
Can I come in, my Bey?

389
00:55:24,769 --> 00:55:26,389
Come, son.

390
00:55:46,455 --> 00:55:48,085
I am sorry.

391
00:55:49,347 --> 00:55:52,937
If I am allowed, I would want to sit.

392
00:56:33,416 --> 00:56:38,196
Tell us, Dündar, what else did
you talk about with Nikola?

393
00:56:41,650 --> 00:56:44,290
I know where Möngke, your son is!

394
00:56:44,394 --> 00:56:45,274
Stop!

395
00:57:03,696 --> 00:57:05,086
Bring him...

396
00:57:06,536 --> 00:57:09,246
... to my tent.

397
00:57:29,585 --> 00:57:30,935
Leave.

398
00:58:21,919 --> 00:58:26,669
Nikola already knew that
Geyhatu was coming, my Bey.

399
00:58:26,669 --> 00:58:28,489
He has spies everywhere.

400
00:58:29,401 --> 00:58:32,771
He signed the agreement anyway?

401
00:58:33,095 --> 00:58:37,095
He said " While Geyhatu is coming,
we wouldn't backstab you...

402
00:58:37,095 --> 00:58:41,975
... be sure of it.
So I sign this agreement."

403
00:58:47,974 --> 00:58:52,474
My Dündar Bey went to that
infidel just in time, my Bey.

404
00:58:52,474 --> 00:58:56,024
At least we have our back safe.

405
00:58:56,071 --> 00:59:00,071
Don't be so sure about it, aunt.

406
00:59:00,499 --> 00:59:05,749
Emperor gave Nikola the
mission to retake those lands.

407
00:59:09,186 --> 00:59:10,636
What about it?

408
00:59:10,636 --> 00:59:12,976
He killed Inegöl's Lord
the moment he came.

409
00:59:15,231 --> 00:59:19,491
He could've used the equipments
he tried to bring here...

410
00:59:19,691 --> 00:59:24,561
... to take Kulucahisar,
Karacahisar and then Söğüt.

411
00:59:25,679 --> 00:59:27,929
When we are weakest.

412
00:59:29,554 --> 00:59:32,514
No one suspects that, Osman.

413
00:59:33,563 --> 00:59:36,913
We will always be watchful.

414
00:59:36,913 --> 00:59:38,923
This is not enough, uncle.

415
00:59:40,098 --> 00:59:42,598
What should we do then, nephew?

416
00:59:52,508 --> 00:59:54,698
We should've striked Nikola harder...

417
00:59:55,784 --> 00:59:59,634
... while he was trapped on a corner.

418
01:00:00,664 --> 01:00:03,154
While Geyhatu is coming to us?

419
01:00:08,063 --> 01:00:12,063
Speak, Osman, what are you thinking?

420
01:00:18,878 --> 01:00:23,698
They will use this "An eye for an eye"
agreement as a weapon.

421
01:00:24,705 --> 01:00:26,105
Sooner or later.

422
01:00:26,334 --> 01:00:28,084
Aren't you Beys?

423
01:00:30,582 --> 01:00:34,142
You will keep your eyes open, so that...

424
01:00:34,616 --> 01:00:37,196
... he wouldn't hit you
in your weak spot...

425
01:00:38,100 --> 01:00:40,870
... he wouldn't punish you
for your sweet dreams.

426
01:00:44,594 --> 01:00:46,354
That's enough.

427
01:00:46,947 --> 01:00:51,927
Lena, bring more of your delicious food.

428
01:00:54,803 --> 01:00:56,763
I will, father.

429
01:01:02,803 --> 01:01:05,973
Where is my son, Möngke?

430
01:01:05,973 --> 01:01:09,273
You will learn when I bring him to you.

431
01:01:17,300 --> 01:01:19,440
You are lying!

432
01:01:21,819 --> 01:01:25,939
If you don't tell his place,
at least tell us who did it.

433
01:01:26,710 --> 01:01:30,210
Or you will get out of this
tent impaled on a stake.

434
01:01:31,852 --> 01:01:35,452
If your dog stays silent,
I have words for you, Geyhatu.

435
01:01:50,605 --> 01:01:56,485
Those who abducted your son,
are the ones who are waiting to end you.

436
01:01:56,485 --> 01:01:57,485
Know that.

437
01:02:01,673 --> 01:02:06,393
He is just like Osman.
Tells 40 lies on foot, 80 on the ground.

438
01:02:06,526 --> 01:02:07,766
Shut up!

439
01:02:16,208 --> 01:02:19,708
Who are those that want to end me?

440
01:02:20,332 --> 01:02:23,132
The ones who know they
can't deal with you in Konya...

441
01:02:23,837 --> 01:02:27,007
... and wants to waste you and
your army away from Konya.

442
01:02:29,425 --> 01:02:35,805
What does that mean? Spit
that poison you hid behind your teeth!

443
01:02:36,009 --> 01:02:37,299
Speak!

444
01:02:37,975 --> 01:02:41,835
You should learn the truth from the ones
who blamed this on my brother, Geyhatu.

445
01:02:42,725 --> 01:02:47,665
I know very well that my brother is
innocent, and where your son is.

446
01:02:47,883 --> 01:02:51,673
But, I will prove that
when I bring him to you.

447
01:02:52,116 --> 01:02:53,896
Give me 3 days.

448
01:02:57,687 --> 01:03:01,687
How do you know that my son is not dead?

449
01:03:03,468 --> 01:03:05,328
I know my brother, Osman.

450
01:03:06,106 --> 01:03:09,946
If he had captured your son
when he attacked your Tent...

451
01:03:10,290 --> 01:03:14,100
... he would've already ripped
his heart, and sent his head to you.

452
01:03:14,711 --> 01:03:17,161
Just like he sent Subutay's head to you.

453
01:03:23,386 --> 01:03:27,036
But, I am grateful that...

454
01:03:27,482 --> 01:03:29,822
... my brother doesn't have your son.

455
01:03:30,140 --> 01:03:33,070
I know he is alive,
and the place they keep him.

456
01:03:33,276 --> 01:03:36,896
Give me 3 days, Geyhatu, only 3 days.

457
01:03:37,124 --> 01:03:38,894
I will bring your son to you.

458
01:03:46,537 --> 01:03:50,927
Do you know what will
happen if you are lying?

459
01:03:52,250 --> 01:03:54,980
I know what will happen to Kayıs,
but you don't know...

460
01:03:55,666 --> 01:03:58,096
... what will happen to you, Geyhatu.

461
01:04:00,313 --> 01:04:03,803
You will be at war with
my father, far from Konya.

462
01:04:04,756 --> 01:04:10,036
In this war, neither my father give Osman
to you, nor you can have your son, Möngke.

463
01:04:10,398 --> 01:04:13,488
Both sides will fight
until the last drop of blood.

464
01:04:13,755 --> 01:04:19,775
Just like you trying to save your son,
I want to save my Tent from your wrath.

465
01:04:19,934 --> 01:04:23,934
But, if something happens
to me or to my Tent...

466
01:04:24,138 --> 01:04:29,158
... then first your son,
then you will pay for it.

467
01:04:29,464 --> 01:04:31,114
Why me?

468
01:04:31,165 --> 01:04:35,745
Because they are not interested in your
son. It's about Ilkhanate's throne!

469
01:04:35,891 --> 01:04:40,941
This is not our war, Geyhatu.
This is Mongols' fight for dynasty!

470
01:04:41,631 --> 01:04:46,201
They want you to fight
us by blaming Osman.

471
01:04:47,608 --> 01:04:52,218
Keep your eyes open, Geyhatu.
These are my words.

472
01:04:56,011 --> 01:04:59,071
This Kayı wants to fool you, Geyhatu.

473
01:04:59,211 --> 01:05:00,111
Shut up!

474
01:05:07,459 --> 01:05:12,939
Know what I'll do, Turk!
I will go to Söğüt with my army...

475
01:05:13,033 --> 01:05:18,753
... to kill all your family,
and to take my son back!

476
01:05:20,960 --> 01:05:24,170
I give you three days!

477
01:05:24,902 --> 01:05:29,932
Three days! Three days!

478
01:05:33,090 --> 01:05:37,810
Then, I will be in Söğüt with my army.

479
01:05:37,810 --> 01:05:42,620
Either you will bring me my son back...

480
01:05:42,791 --> 01:05:43,751
... or...

481
01:06:25,493 --> 01:06:27,194
Listen to me carefully.

482
01:08:00,307 --> 01:08:02,351
Ya Allah!

483
01:08:15,488 --> 01:08:18,865
With the name of Allah!
Ya Allah!

484
01:09:38,330 --> 01:09:40,144
With the name of Allah!

485
01:09:59,056 --> 01:10:02,389
A secret doesn't get revealed.

486
01:10:02,815 --> 01:10:06,781
A secret makes love with the
roots of the trees...

487
01:10:07,184 --> 01:10:10,159
...seven feet underground.

488
01:10:13,037 --> 01:10:14,696
It makes love but...

489
01:10:14,966 --> 01:10:16,875
...it doesn't get revealed.

490
01:10:29,672 --> 01:10:34,639
A dream of building a state isn't easy...

491
01:10:35,264 --> 01:10:37,331
...it isn't easy.

492
01:10:37,531 --> 01:10:43,598
Wen the need shows up, the truth reveals
itself like the sun...

493
01:10:44,023 --> 01:10:48,390
...then the secrets get revealed too.

494
01:11:16,255 --> 01:11:18,967
I, Bamsı Beyrek...

495
01:11:19,193 --> 01:11:22,762
...mountains, steppes were too
little for me...

496
01:11:22,762 --> 01:11:25,638
...but I lived underground for
too long.

497
01:11:26,791 --> 01:11:29,748
Now, there is a need...

498
01:11:30,132 --> 01:11:33,470
...now, it's time to make
the dream true.

499
01:12:35,336 --> 01:12:39,401
My holy valiant, my faithful friend...

500
01:12:39,990 --> 01:12:42,412
...Ertuğrul Bey...

501
01:12:43,258 --> 01:12:47,565
...now is the time to realize a dream.

502
01:13:01,800 --> 01:13:04,285
Ya Allah!

503
01:13:05,337 --> 01:13:07,523
Ya Allah!

504
01:13:08,759 --> 01:13:11,208
Ya Allah!

505
01:14:31,186 --> 01:14:34,126
Take care of yourself.
Get well soon.

506
01:14:36,025 --> 01:14:37,981
Be careful for a little
while longer.

507
01:14:39,168 --> 01:14:43,232
Lena, these were the last of the
medicines.

508
01:14:43,232 --> 01:14:48,808
We got rid of the plague, Gonca.
We can make new ones if needed.

509
01:14:49,533 --> 01:14:55,004
With Dündar Bey's efforts and your
experience, we are good now.

510
01:14:58,253 --> 01:15:02,582
Keep it in your mouth for a while. Don't
swallow it. It will give you strength.

511
01:15:02,582 --> 01:15:04,432
Rest at home for a while.

512
01:15:04,432 --> 01:15:09,796
Bala is a solid person, too. It's a good thing
that she shared her knowledge with you.

513
01:15:09,881 --> 01:15:13,819
Many lives were saved with the medicines
you made.

514
01:15:14,032 --> 01:15:17,229
-May Allah bless you both.
-Thank you.

515
01:15:29,933 --> 01:15:34,606
You did a lot, as well, Gonca Hatun.
Look how you wish for good.

516
01:15:41,518 --> 01:15:44,058
Remember, the best medicine is love.

517
01:16:22,779 --> 01:16:26,380
Gonca Hatun, I will check the horses
and come back.

518
01:16:26,763 --> 01:16:29,919
Start the preparations.
I'll be back in a moment.

519
01:17:33,369 --> 01:17:35,756
What do you want?

520
01:17:46,546 --> 01:17:48,700
Trails end here.

521
01:18:26,453 --> 01:18:27,894
Give an order, my bey.

522
01:18:35,363 --> 01:18:38,773
You didn't change your name
or your religion.

523
01:18:38,873 --> 01:18:42,593
I didn't forget who I am,
I won't.

524
01:18:45,028 --> 01:18:47,108
It's not too late.

525
01:18:49,197 --> 01:18:51,693
I have a son at the same height as you.

526
01:18:52,650 --> 01:18:58,025
Everyone makes mistakes.
I still love you, Lena.

527
01:19:04,152 --> 01:19:09,331
Dying at your hands?
It'd be nice.

528
01:19:17,908 --> 01:19:21,402
My soldiers...

529
01:19:25,564 --> 01:19:29,322
If you don't want to die by the hands
of my first and only love...

530
01:19:30,176 --> 01:19:33,047
...don't face me again...

531
01:19:33,117 --> 01:19:35,582
...you hound.

532
01:19:43,693 --> 01:19:45,871
Sooner or later, Lena.

533
01:19:55,806 --> 01:19:57,552
Where is Möngke?

534
01:19:59,934 --> 01:20:01,931
You didn't know where he is...

535
01:20:02,318 --> 01:20:04,892
...you played us and Geyhatu.

536
01:20:09,572 --> 01:20:14,721
-Who are you and where is Möngke?
-ı wouldn't tell you even if I knew.

537
01:20:37,616 --> 01:20:39,213
Where is Möngke?

538
01:20:48,261 --> 01:20:53,620
-Where is Möngke?
-All right, enough! I will tell you!

539
01:20:55,672 --> 01:20:57,019
I'll tell you.

540
01:20:59,474 --> 01:21:07,585
I swear I don't know where he is.
Just in Blacksea, at a dead harbor.

541
01:21:08,354 --> 01:21:12,414
They are hiding him underground,
in a cellar.

542
01:21:13,669 --> 01:21:15,466
Yes.

543
01:21:54,273 --> 01:21:56,286
This pot is full, Ahmed.

544
01:21:59,708 --> 01:22:02,243
Put it on the fire.

545
01:22:06,060 --> 01:22:07,422
What happened to you?

546
01:22:09,668 --> 01:22:11,613
Tell me, Ahmed.

547
01:22:20,742 --> 01:22:24,150
Why is Ertuğrul bey treating Osman Bey
like that?

548
01:22:29,731 --> 01:22:35,127
What kind of words is those, Ahmed?
Ertuğrul Bey's sons are his pieces.

549
01:22:36,486 --> 01:22:39,260
Why would he trreat Osman Bey badly?

550
01:22:39,260 --> 01:22:42,654
Wasn't it Osman Bey who saved our
tents from the Mongols?

551
01:22:42,760 --> 01:22:45,630
Isn't he the one who conquered
Kulucahisar?

552
01:22:50,868 --> 01:22:53,435
Come on, let's put the pot on the fire.

553
01:22:53,987 --> 01:22:57,558
-Osman Bey
-Ahmed Alp.

554
01:23:03,147 --> 01:23:05,454
Ahmed, put this pot on the fire.

555
01:23:13,798 --> 01:23:17,896
Even this little child knows.
But my father doesn't.

556
01:23:20,624 --> 01:23:23,694
You can talk to your father tonight,
Osman.

557
01:23:24,294 --> 01:23:28,591
Ertuğrul Bey is your father.
He will listen to you.

558
01:23:29,143 --> 01:23:31,902
Just try to talk to him.

559
01:24:24,436 --> 01:24:28,591
My bey! My bey!
Help me, they'll kill my father!

560
01:24:28,591 --> 01:24:31,767
-Where is he, show me!
-This way, my bey.

561
01:24:40,601 --> 01:24:42,131
Have you had enough fun?

562
01:24:46,330 --> 01:24:47,981
Get up, brother!

563
01:24:50,495 --> 01:24:53,614
-Thank you, Turk!
-You want some, Turk?

564
01:24:54,437 --> 01:24:56,271
Don't meddle.

565
01:25:09,094 --> 01:25:12,495
Put that dagger down.
There will be no blood.

566
01:25:13,071 --> 01:25:14,603
Die, Turk!

567
01:25:35,795 --> 01:25:38,887
Enough, enough, enough!

568
01:25:41,338 --> 01:25:43,098
Enough!

569
01:25:46,200 --> 01:25:51,586
-What's happening here, Göktuğ?
-These three were beating the Rum.

570
01:25:54,738 --> 01:25:58,116
-I intervened.
-We had a bet.

571
01:25:58,551 --> 01:26:02,159
We had no problem before this
Turk showing up.

572
01:26:03,420 --> 01:26:07,406
It's true, my bey.
I didn't understand it, either.

573
01:26:07,622 --> 01:26:10,509
This alp attacked unarmed guards
with his dagger.

574
01:26:14,706 --> 01:26:19,535
-Lying dog! Lying dog!
-Göktuğ!

575
01:26:27,872 --> 01:26:31,462
-He is losing too much blood.
-Take him to the public house.

576
01:26:32,255 --> 01:26:34,335
Call the physicians.

577
01:26:39,862 --> 01:26:42,903
Dündar Bey, these dogs are lying!

578
01:26:45,871 --> 01:26:49,630
While your lord is signing a peace
deal with Lord Nicola...

579
01:26:50,131 --> 01:26:53,008
...you are stabbing us from the
back here, Dündar Bey.

580
01:26:55,625 --> 01:26:58,672
I'll find out what happened, Vladius.
I will.

581
01:26:58,696 --> 01:27:01,287
You attacked my armless soldiers.

582
01:27:03,098 --> 01:27:05,088
La Hawla.
(Wishing patience)

583
01:27:06,489 --> 01:27:10,919
You must avoid imputating which you
are going to regret later, Vladius.

584
01:27:11,366 --> 01:27:15,866
Ertuğrul Bey should pay for my soldier's
life.

585
01:27:16,039 --> 01:27:19,599
Tit-for-tat, Dündar Bey.

586
01:27:19,693 --> 01:27:21,863
- You liar!
- Göktüğ!

587
01:27:24,181 --> 01:27:26,211
Göktuğ!

588
01:27:29,254 --> 01:27:32,934
I am not like an armless soldier,
you Mongol offspring!

589
01:27:36,061 --> 01:27:37,331
Göktuğ!

590
01:27:37,488 --> 01:27:40,898
- I will cut your tongue!
- Göktuğ!

591
01:27:40,950 --> 01:27:44,850
- I'll kill you!
- Calm down! calm down!

592
01:27:45,909 --> 01:27:47,939
Calm down!

593
01:27:52,241 --> 01:27:56,311
Take him to dungeon.
Take his swords away.

594
01:27:56,884 --> 01:28:00,674
Ertuğrul Bey will decide what will happen.

595
01:28:21,775 --> 01:28:27,115
If something happens to my soldier,
you'll pay for it.

596
01:28:27,169 --> 01:28:29,209
Dündar Bey.

597
01:29:00,930 --> 01:29:05,250
Do you know the story of the cat with
stomped tail?

598
01:29:05,259 --> 01:29:08,179
What happened to the cat?

599
01:29:09,907 --> 01:29:12,606
She lost her food.

600
01:29:12,606 --> 01:29:15,426
What are you talking about?

601
01:29:16,064 --> 01:29:20,884
-Tell me what happened.
-Osman Bey's coming, don't you understand?

602
01:29:21,214 --> 01:29:26,584
He shall come. We have cold
ayran(a beverage) and a good talk.

603
01:29:27,959 --> 01:29:33,369
I'm saying that things will get crazy,
and you're talkin about ayran? I'm leaving

604
01:29:33,387 --> 01:29:35,497
Wait.

605
01:29:37,020 --> 01:29:41,868
- Tell me what it is.
- Ertuğrul Bey has news from Söğütlü.

606
01:29:41,888 --> 01:29:46,148
When Osman Bey hears about it, he'll
go mad, Master Davut.

607
01:29:46,208 --> 01:29:48,950
Here he is.
What are we going to say?

608
01:29:48,950 --> 01:29:52,740
We know what we have to do.

609
01:29:52,740 --> 01:29:56,870
Tell it to Osman Bey then.
In a proper way!

610
01:30:02,139 --> 01:30:05,819
- Salam Alaikum.
- Alaikum Salam.

611
01:30:13,383 --> 01:30:16,323
What happened?
You look pale.

612
01:30:16,757 --> 01:30:19,797
You're out of breath.

613
01:30:25,260 --> 01:30:27,680
Tell me.

614
01:30:28,882 --> 01:30:32,640
Göktuğ Bey injured Nikola's
unarmed soldier in Söğüt.

615
01:30:32,640 --> 01:30:38,386
Soldier is losing blood. Dündar Bey sent
him to dungeon. They want tit for tat.

616
01:30:38,386 --> 01:30:44,516
If the soldier dies, they say Göktuğ
will be executed, my Bey.

617
01:31:03,850 --> 01:31:10,340
What have you done, İdris?
You told it all in once!

618
01:31:10,924 --> 01:31:13,614
May Allah grant us with the good.

619
01:31:42,127 --> 01:31:43,987
Can I come in, my Bey?

620
01:31:44,751 --> 01:31:46,851
Come in, son.

621
01:32:05,825 --> 01:32:10,485
I know you are young and excited.
I understand that.

622
01:32:12,070 --> 01:32:15,470
I don't want to be rebel, my father.

623
01:32:16,015 --> 01:32:19,988
We all knew Nikola would do something
villainy.

624
01:32:19,988 --> 01:32:21,838
What is going to happen now father?

625
01:32:22,162 --> 01:32:27,242
I warned you to be careful!
You couldn't take care of your Alp Göktuğ.

626
01:32:28,228 --> 01:32:30,516
You put me in a difficult situation, Osman.

627
01:32:30,516 --> 01:32:35,396
Göktuğ is in dungeon.
What is going to happen now father?

628
01:32:36,519 --> 01:32:41,589
Are you going to let my Alp die
because of the rule tit for that?

629
01:32:42,511 --> 01:32:47,801
Don't you know that I am going to do what
I have to do if he is guilty, Osman?

630
01:32:49,144 --> 01:32:51,894
Father, how can you say this?

631
01:32:52,020 --> 01:32:54,465
Aren't you Ertuğrul Bey?

632
01:32:54,465 --> 01:32:59,945
We offered this agreement. They accepted.

633
01:33:01,476 --> 01:33:06,636
And you men ruined everything in
the first day!

634
01:33:06,844 --> 01:33:11,304
Osman, who can't take care of his Alps!

635
01:33:13,490 --> 01:33:15,670
I conquered castles with my Alps.

636
01:33:16,460 --> 01:33:21,490
I defeated the enemy when you
were not here.

637
01:33:21,609 --> 01:33:26,869
They didn't go behind my back like my
uncle or my brother.

638
01:33:27,334 --> 01:33:30,474
Get over it, Osman!

639
01:33:35,023 --> 01:33:41,243
While bothering with Beyhatu, you opened
a new war.

640
01:33:42,229 --> 01:33:46,129
Your Alps ruined the game I had been
planning.

641
01:33:49,105 --> 01:33:50,995
Father.

642
01:33:54,100 --> 01:33:56,100
Father...

643
01:34:05,263 --> 01:34:08,233
Are you really Ertuğrul Bey?

644
01:34:13,876 --> 01:34:15,956
His very self!

645
01:34:17,543 --> 01:34:21,483
Do not ever interfere in this issue.

646
01:34:22,077 --> 01:34:27,007
Or, it will cost you dearly.

647
01:35:03,654 --> 01:35:06,264
What have I done, father?

648
01:35:09,973 --> 01:35:13,203
What have I done to fall from
your grace?

649
01:35:15,020 --> 01:35:19,870
In Beyship position, there's
no son and father. You should know that.

650
01:35:20,944 --> 01:35:25,644
Our first objective is our tribe's peace.

651
01:35:58,915 --> 01:36:01,895
Son is the secret of father.

652
01:36:04,423 --> 01:36:08,983
Ararya Hadrat was right to state this
sentence..

653
01:36:34,801 --> 01:36:37,757
I like good news, Vladius.

654
01:36:37,757 --> 01:36:41,485
- Tell it to me with joy!
- Just like what we thought.

655
01:36:41,485 --> 01:36:44,245
Göktuğ ate the bait.

656
01:36:47,579 --> 01:36:50,500
You should have seen Göktuğ and Dündar's
despair, Nikola.

657
01:36:50,500 --> 01:36:57,090
When Ertuğrul learns this, he will be
bad with Osman.

658
01:36:57,652 --> 01:36:59,581
Of course.

659
01:36:59,581 --> 01:37:04,111
What is the condition of
the wounded soldier?

660
01:37:06,631 --> 01:37:08,981
He is not wounded anymore.

661
01:37:10,669 --> 01:37:12,531
What do you mean.

662
01:37:12,531 --> 01:37:15,271
I made the game more covincing.

663
01:37:16,277 --> 01:37:18,521
How did you do it?

664
01:37:18,521 --> 01:37:20,761
I killed him.

665
01:37:29,941 --> 01:37:35,131
Well played.
You drove Osman's Alp crazy

666
01:37:36,125 --> 01:37:39,085
You deserve this.

667
01:37:43,955 --> 01:37:48,405
I am happy to serve you, even though
I'm hurt.

668
01:37:53,053 --> 01:37:55,353
Good job.

669
01:38:22,643 --> 01:38:24,593
Soldier!

670
01:38:29,416 --> 01:38:34,156
Go want justice for our death soldier!

671
01:38:34,652 --> 01:38:37,362
Collect the gold also.

672
01:38:37,475 --> 01:38:40,395
They will find his body.

673
01:38:56,535 --> 01:39:01,515
Send you spies to Söğütlü from now,
Vladius.

674
01:39:04,163 --> 01:39:07,443
Osman will want to save his Alp.

675
01:39:07,801 --> 01:39:11,671
Try not to face him.

676
01:39:12,838 --> 01:39:17,608
If necessary, ambush him.

677
01:39:22,580 --> 01:39:26,970
And never ever never...

678
01:39:27,291 --> 01:39:34,261
do something without my knowledge
and go beyond my orders!

679
01:40:02,979 --> 01:40:06,638
- Is it right, Boran?
- Yes, my Bey.

680
01:40:06,638 --> 01:40:11,099
Göktuğ is in dungeon. His life is dependent
on Ertuğrul Bey an Nikola!

681
01:40:11,099 --> 01:40:13,939
There is something wrong with this!

682
01:40:14,029 --> 01:40:16,239
Absolutely.

683
01:40:19,294 --> 01:40:23,504
- Göktuğ doesn't kill someone armless.
- I know, my Bey.

684
01:40:25,896 --> 01:40:28,616
We will save Göktuğ from dungeon.

685
01:40:28,650 --> 01:40:31,690
Are we going to disobey Ertuğrul Bey?

686
01:40:31,977 --> 01:40:36,037
Nikola wants to put my father in a
difficult position.

687
01:40:36,151 --> 01:40:38,981
We won't let this.

688
01:40:40,203 --> 01:40:43,243
Nikola and Vladius will come to Söğüt,
my Bey.

689
01:40:43,282 --> 01:40:45,622
We need to do it before they come.

690
01:40:47,052 --> 01:40:49,852
Lİsten tomecarefully name.

691
01:41:51,917 --> 01:41:53,587
Be ready!

692
01:42:24,438 --> 01:42:28,198
My Bey, these are dressed like the others.

693
01:42:28,201 --> 01:42:30,581
It's not clear that whose dogs are they.

694
01:42:30,630 --> 01:42:35,460
Pigeons brought us the nest of snakes.
Hold on.

695
01:42:35,563 --> 01:42:37,613
Eyvallah (okay) my Bey.

696
01:43:27,394 --> 01:43:30,404
I am not a killer.

697
01:43:33,604 --> 01:43:36,424
I am not a killer.

698
01:43:37,048 --> 01:43:39,008
I am not.

699
01:43:51,957 --> 01:43:55,107
Stop!
Who are you?

700
01:44:00,924 --> 01:44:03,528
Alps!
Alps!

701
01:44:03,528 --> 01:44:08,318
Who are you? Let alps be free!
Come to me!

702
01:44:08,540 --> 01:44:12,300
Come to me! Who are you!

703
01:44:20,904 --> 01:44:23,404
Abdurrahman Ghazi!

704
01:44:23,484 --> 01:44:25,774
My valiant!

705
01:44:40,545 --> 01:44:42,915
Abdurrahman Ghazi!

706
01:44:43,524 --> 01:44:45,994
Masha Allah(praise be) my valiant.

707
01:44:51,285 --> 01:44:56,435
After Geyhatu issue passes, Osman Bey
will hide you.

708
01:44:59,563 --> 01:45:04,240
Eyvallah (thank you) Abdurrahman Ghazi.
I am here under the order of my Ertuğrul Bey.

709
01:45:04,240 --> 01:45:06,660
Even if there's death in the end, I won't
leave.

710
01:45:07,112 --> 01:45:12,292
My lion, do I ever disobey Ertuğrul Bey?

711
01:45:15,157 --> 01:45:18,127
Is there Ertuğrul Bey behind this?

712
01:45:18,233 --> 01:45:24,023
Come on. without drawing atteniton,
leave Söğüt, find Osman Bey.

713
01:45:24,436 --> 01:45:25,726
Come on.

714
01:45:25,999 --> 01:45:28,679
Eyvallah (thank you) Abdurrahman Ghazi.

715
01:45:28,685 --> 01:45:30,575
Eyvallah (okay) my lion.

716
01:46:51,267 --> 01:46:53,617
Is it true, Leyla?

717
01:46:54,328 --> 01:46:58,988
We were just getting over the plague,
and those came up!

718
01:47:00,745 --> 01:47:04,955
This Göktuğ put my Ertuğrul Bey
in a difficult situation.

719
01:47:05,661 --> 01:47:07,925
Like Osman was not enough!

720
01:47:07,925 --> 01:47:12,535
Our Ertuğrul Bey will surely protect
Göktuğ.

721
01:47:12,535 --> 01:47:17,215
- Don't be sure about that.
- Hazal Hatun is right, Bala.

722
01:47:18,581 --> 01:47:21,013
I don;'t understand.

723
01:47:21,013 --> 01:47:23,969
Göktuğ wouldn't kill an unarmed soldier.

724
01:47:23,969 --> 01:47:29,839
Even if this is true, Ertuğrul Bey has
made an agreement with Nikola.

725
01:47:29,965 --> 01:47:33,472
Be sure that he will remain true to
his word.

726
01:47:33,472 --> 01:47:38,255
It is Osman's battle friend
Göktuğ we are talking about, Hazal Hatun

727
01:47:38,915 --> 01:47:43,545
Put Göktuğ aside, even if it was Osman...

728
01:47:43,545 --> 01:47:47,425
Ertuğrul Bey wouldn't retract
his agreement.

729
01:48:11,736 --> 01:48:13,116
Who are they?

730
01:48:16,866 --> 01:48:17,966
Who are you?!

731
01:48:43,460 --> 01:48:47,460
- I'll take you to Geyhatu.
- Why are you doing this, Turk?

732
01:48:53,698 --> 01:48:56,248
Not for your life.

733
01:49:03,748 --> 01:49:05,658
Fight for your life.

734
01:49:17,525 --> 01:49:20,005
What I heard are true, Dündar Bey?

735
01:49:21,157 --> 01:49:22,237
Yes.

736
01:49:23,227 --> 01:49:26,547
Göktuğ Alp argued with
one of your soldiers.

737
01:49:26,695 --> 01:49:30,695
Then a death happened.

738
01:49:31,199 --> 01:49:34,269
But my soldier died.

739
01:49:35,194 --> 01:49:36,894
In your city.

740
01:49:37,708 --> 01:49:40,038
There will be a response to this.

741
01:49:40,190 --> 01:49:44,190
It wasn't intentional, you
should know that.

742
01:49:45,840 --> 01:49:47,790
What have we talked about?

743
01:49:48,497 --> 01:49:50,727
An eye for an eye.

744
01:49:51,614 --> 01:49:54,834
I like people
who keep their words, Dündar Bey.

745
01:49:55,218 --> 01:49:57,028
Where is Ertuğrul Bey?

746
01:49:57,231 --> 01:50:01,231
He's in his room, waiting for you.

747
01:50:37,104 --> 01:50:39,994
Osman Bey is on his way.

748
01:50:42,392 --> 01:50:44,102
Just as I want.

749
01:50:44,672 --> 01:50:47,272
- Are his Alps (men) with him?
- No, he's alone.

750
01:50:49,996 --> 01:50:52,326
It's time to payoff, Osman.

751
01:50:55,218 --> 01:50:56,238
Let's go.

752
01:51:17,869 --> 01:51:19,419
Can I come in, my Bey?

753
01:51:20,699 --> 01:51:22,319
Come in.

754
01:51:25,820 --> 01:51:28,440
Nikola, Governor of
Yenigöl Castle, is here.

755
01:51:40,130 --> 01:51:42,780
Whenever I make an agreement with you...

756
01:51:43,357 --> 01:51:45,867
I'm hurt, Ertuğrul Bey.

757
01:51:46,866 --> 01:51:50,176
I heard what happened, Governor Nikola.

758
01:51:52,199 --> 01:51:54,139
My condolences.

759
01:51:55,502 --> 01:51:59,502
- May rest in peace.
- Your Alp, who didn't listen to your orders...

760
01:52:01,329 --> 01:52:03,969
killed my young soldier.

761
01:52:09,398 --> 01:52:10,748
Ertuğrul Bey.

762
01:52:11,454 --> 01:52:13,734
My soldiers are angry.

763
01:52:13,901 --> 01:52:15,631
They want the cost.

764
01:52:16,806 --> 01:52:19,036
You know what I mean.

765
01:52:20,143 --> 01:52:22,753
If you don't call out my Alps...

766
01:52:24,820 --> 01:52:27,440
your dignity...

767
01:52:28,040 --> 01:52:31,030
will fall.

768
01:52:32,364 --> 01:52:35,654
I won't let you do this to me again.

769
01:52:36,994 --> 01:52:43,234
Today, if the scaffold isn't ready...

770
01:52:44,141 --> 01:52:46,091
you should know
that you'll fight in...

771
01:52:46,599 --> 01:52:49,439
two fronts, not one.

772
01:52:51,649 --> 01:52:53,549
Can I come in, my Bey?

773
01:52:53,889 --> 01:52:55,199
Come in.

774
01:52:59,142 --> 01:53:02,012
Göktuğ Alp escaped from the dungeon.

775
01:53:16,464 --> 01:53:19,194
What kind of game
are you in, Ertuğrul Bey?

776
01:53:20,939 --> 01:53:23,369
What kind of game is it?

777
01:55:53,750 --> 01:55:54,710
My Bey...

778
01:55:56,657 --> 01:55:58,237
fighting with you...

779
01:56:01,000 --> 01:56:02,390
was an honor, my Bey.

780
01:56:05,340 --> 01:56:07,950
"I bear witness that there is no
deity but Allah..."

781
01:56:09,240 --> 01:56:13,600
"and I bear witness that Muhammad
is the messenger of Allah."

782
01:56:38,512 --> 01:56:39,782
You...

783
01:56:43,692 --> 01:56:46,602
Don't waste your breath, Kayı boy.

784
01:57:19,942 --> 01:57:21,992
Good job, Möngke.

785
01:57:23,997 --> 01:57:25,507
Good job.

786
01:58:14,171 --> 01:58:15,461
Catch him!

787
01:58:43,260 --> 01:58:45,470
I'll kill you, Osman.

788
01:59:15,409 --> 01:59:17,419
I asked a question, Ertuğrul Bey.

789
01:59:18,764 --> 01:59:21,564
Do you want to play a game with me?

790
01:59:22,494 --> 01:59:25,404
Give me the killer of my soldier or...

791
01:59:26,462 --> 01:59:29,782
or I'll take the sword of justice.

792
01:59:32,365 --> 01:59:35,165
One day, Oghuz Khagan went hunting.

793
01:59:36,699 --> 01:59:41,859
He had a deer and tied it to a tree.

794
01:59:42,922 --> 01:59:45,102
You know why?

795
01:59:48,803 --> 01:59:53,023
He wanted to know the monster that
he wanted to hunt.

796
01:59:56,452 --> 01:59:58,312
He came at dawn.

797
01:59:58,817 --> 02:00:00,837
He saw that...

798
02:00:01,871 --> 02:00:04,041
the monster took the deer.

799
02:00:06,223 --> 02:00:08,053
Ertuğrul Bey.

800
02:00:12,222 --> 02:00:14,412
What do you mean?

801
02:00:14,828 --> 02:00:19,768
Drink this sherbet and take a breath.

802
02:00:20,865 --> 02:00:24,865
There is good stuff in the Turk's sagas.

803
02:00:25,905 --> 02:00:28,335
You'll be good.

804
02:01:47,193 --> 02:01:49,163
You can't run away, Osman!

805
02:01:50,254 --> 02:01:53,244
These lands will be your grave!

806
02:01:57,772 --> 02:01:59,812
This time, Oghuz Khagan...

807
02:02:01,487 --> 02:02:04,697
tied himself to that tree.

808
02:02:07,833 --> 02:02:09,853
He waited.

809
02:02:10,488 --> 02:02:12,708
Then the monster came.

810
02:02:14,897 --> 02:02:17,697
Oghuz Khagan hit the monster's head...

811
02:02:18,984 --> 02:02:21,094
and killed him.

812
02:02:21,179 --> 02:02:24,479
He cut its head.

813
02:02:29,193 --> 02:02:30,733
Ertuğrul Bey!

814
02:02:31,326 --> 02:02:34,796
I'm done with these words.
I can't bear them.

815
02:02:38,136 --> 02:02:43,356
I'll raid your rent with my army
if this keeps going like that.

816
02:02:55,430 --> 02:02:57,600
Like Oghuz Khagan's tree...

817
02:02:59,160 --> 02:03:02,320
Söğüt is my only
tree. (the precious thing)

818
02:03:04,310 --> 02:03:09,580
I wait for you there.

819
02:03:11,823 --> 02:03:15,823
Come whenever you want.

820
02:03:20,703 --> 02:03:22,373
Threat?

821
02:03:23,483 --> 02:03:25,723
I don't like threats, Ertuğrul Bey.

822
02:03:28,057 --> 02:03:29,977
An ammunition raid...

823
02:03:30,085 --> 02:03:34,765
then you kill my innocent soldier!

824
02:03:35,214 --> 02:03:38,894
Your sons are
responsible for them!

825
02:03:40,731 --> 02:03:42,281
Ertuğrul Bey.

826
02:03:42,946 --> 02:03:47,566
You can't even look after a killer.

827
02:03:48,507 --> 02:03:52,507
You can't rule neither your Alp...

828
02:03:52,634 --> 02:03:55,144
nor your sons.

829
02:03:57,713 --> 02:04:01,713
Whether you'll give me
the killer of my soldier...

830
02:04:02,651 --> 02:04:07,161
Or you'll pay the price.

831
02:04:25,833 --> 02:04:29,833
Don't you know I keep my words?

832
02:04:31,129 --> 02:04:32,819
When the time comes...

833
02:04:34,482 --> 02:04:38,812
my Alp will be put on trial
in front of everyone.

834
02:04:41,171 --> 02:04:43,691
You'll witness it.

835
02:04:44,414 --> 02:04:46,134
Do you understand me?

836
02:04:55,252 --> 02:04:56,932
By the way...

837
02:04:57,688 --> 02:04:59,958
If something happens to Göktuğ...

838
02:05:01,323 --> 02:05:05,323
you'll see what the payoff is.

839
02:06:12,919 --> 02:06:14,079
He's there.

840
02:06:19,718 --> 02:06:21,248
Osman!

841
02:06:22,615 --> 02:06:24,565
You're trapped, Osman.

842
02:06:27,005 --> 02:06:31,005
Give me the murderer of my soldier! I
want Göktuğ!

843
02:06:31,222 --> 02:06:33,322
I know you abducted him!

844
02:06:33,365 --> 02:06:34,455
Flatyos.

845
02:06:35,783 --> 02:06:38,893
Did your man die from a little bite?

846
02:06:39,399 --> 02:06:41,949
Or from a nightmare?

847
02:06:43,191 --> 02:06:44,851
Tell me.

848
02:06:45,041 --> 02:06:48,711
You're trapped, Osman. Give us Göktuğ!

849
02:06:48,844 --> 02:06:51,804
I made many dogs like you bow down
to me.

850
02:06:52,380 --> 02:06:54,330
Now it's your turn to bow down.

851
02:06:55,030 --> 02:06:56,880
You'll die!

852
02:06:57,756 --> 02:06:59,776
You'll die.

853
02:08:01,243 --> 02:08:02,563
Bamsı Bey.

854
02:08:03,588 --> 02:08:05,298
My Osman.

855
02:08:32,835 --> 02:08:34,435
My Osman.

856
02:08:34,645 --> 02:09:01,715
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com